WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.970
Around 1079, a French monk called Gaunilo
read Anselm's new argument for God.

2
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.330
Gaunilo was himself a believer.

3
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.050
But he thought the logic must be faulty.

4
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.370
So he imagined a lost island, more
excellent than all other lands.

5
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:21.870
If you imagine the perfect
island, must it exist somewhere?

6
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.260
In this mission, you'll see Gaunilo
turn Anselm's logic on the island,

7
00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.490
and how Anselm replied.

8
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.460
Then you'll test the argument
against Immanuel Kant,

9
00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.230
and weigh what it is worth for faith.

10
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.070
Your mission: find out whether imagining
something perfect could ever prove it

11
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:39.810
is real.
